Third-party code, used ONLY by the gas benchmarks of this directory.
This is a MINIMAL EXTRACTION, not a copy of the library.

Upstream : https://github.com/gizatechxyz/orion
Commit   : bac0b424fe08e0da9e2522a45d77c028acf47dcd (v0.2.5, 2025-03-03, targets Cairo 2.5.3)
License  : MIT, Copyright (c) 2023 Auditless Limited (see LICENSE)

Why: orion does not build with Cairo 2.19.4 (125 errors: its own `Div` impls for i8..i128
now collide with corelib's, `consteval_int!` suffix literals, `Store` derive, inference changes,
plus its pinned dependencies alexandria@800f5ad and cubit@6275608 which fail too). The Tensor
machinery is one ~106-method trait implemented for 11 element types, spread over 244 source files
(108 for the tensor operators alone); porting it was out of the time box.

Verbatim files (byte-identical to upstream, except the corelib 2.20.0 patch below):
  - src/numbers/fixed_point/core.cairo, utils.cairo
  - src/numbers/fixed_point/implementations/{fp16x16,fp32x32,fp64x64}{.cairo,/**}
  - src/operators/tensor/linalg/matmul.cairo

Corelib 2.20.0 patch (TC2-LIBS, 2026-11-13): `core::integer::u32_as_non_zero` was removed. Each
`integer::u32_as_non_zero(x)` became `x.try_into().unwrap()` (corelib's TryInto<T, NonZero<T>>,
which also panics on zero; every argument is a non-zero constant): 8 call sites, in
src/numbers/fixed_point/implementations/fp16x16/math/{core,trig}.cairo. Same results: the 64 unit
tests pass before (2.19.4) and after (2.20.1); Sierra gas moves only by the toolchain's offset.

Verbatim with one marked PATCH:
  - src/operators/vec.cairo: `VecTrait` (from alexandria_data_structures@800f5ad) inlined.

Extracted files (function bodies verbatim, everything not needed by the benchmarks dropped,
each file says so in its header):
  - src/numbers.cairo                    NumberTrait reduced to `zero()`, impls for FP16x16/FP32x32
  - src/operators/tensor/core.cairo      Tensor<T>, TensorTrait reduced to new/at/add/matmul,
                                         new_tensor, ravel_index, unravel_index, stride, at_tensor
  - src/operators/tensor/helpers.cairo   len_from_shape, check_shape, check_compatibility,
                                         broadcast_index_mapping*, broadcast_shape
  - src/operators/tensor/math/arithmetic.cairo   `add` (broadcasting element-wise add)
  - src/operators/tensor/implementations/tensor_fp{16x16,32x32}.cairo   the 4 kept methods
  - src/operators/matrix.cairo           MutMatrix up to `shape` (argmax/softmax/sigmoid dropped)
  - src/utils.cairo                      u32_max + `reverse` (alexandria SpanTraitExt::reverse@800f5ad)
  - module files (lib.cairo, numbers/fixed_point.cairo, operators*.cairo, ...) rewritten.

The `cubit` dependency (upstream pin 6275608) points to the vendored ../cubit (8007a30): the f64 /
f128 add/mul/div/sqrt/trig code that FP32x32 / FP64x64 delegate to is functionally identical
between the two revisions (only `u64_wide_mul` -> `WideMul::wide_mul`, `u128_sqrt` -> `Sqrt::sqrt`).
